# charon integration step 35 after 546078ea5d: commit 5bb203828ea85c38ca598124abaabb68d5cec4b1
# first parent a112a3e826edf400722d95d92436629cd56a2ad3
# series charon-ml: patch -p1 in the root of the upstream source
#
# charon-ml: crate_of_file decodes an llbc file without its whole JSON tree
#
# Yojson.Basic.from_file builds the tree of the whole file, which takes about 7 times the file size
# (chelis-deep: 1.4 GB for 186 MB) while the decoded crate takes 1 GB less. crate_of_file reads the
# file with Yojson's lexer: the top-level objects field by field, and the lists of `translated`
# (files, name tables, item tables) one element at a time, with the same element decoders as
# crate_of_json, in serialization order. It fails like crate_of_json on anything else (wrong field
# order, unknown or missing field, trailing data).
#
# The deserialization test checks that both decoders give the same crate on every ui llbc.

